<title>USA: N. Carolina Treasurer Boyles wins re-election.</title>
<headline>N. Carolina Treasurer Boyles wins re-election.</headline>
<dateline>RALEIGH, N.C. 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Longtime North Carolina Treasurer Harlan Boyles easily won re-election in Tuesday's voting, state treasury officials said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Boyles, 66, is a Democrat who has had charge of state coffers for 20 years. He defeated Republican candidate Ann Duncan, who previously headed the state Employment Security Commission.</p>
<p>--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013</p>
</text>
